Rupam Sahoo was born in West Bengal, India. He received his B.Sc. (Honors) degree in Chemistry from Visva-Bharati University, India, in 2016. After completing his M.Sc. degree in July 2018 with inorganic specialization from the same university, Rupam has joined Framework Lab as a Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR) fellow under the supervision of Prof. Madhab C. Das at the Indian Institute of Technology, Kharagpur for his PhD research work. His thesis work focuses on the designs and synthesis of acid ligand-based ultra-stable metal–organic frameworks for their suitable potential application in hydrocarbon separations and proton conduction domain.
Supriya Mondal was born in West Bengal, India. She received her B.Sc. (Hons) degree in Chemistry from Bankura Christian College, India, in 2017. She completed her M.Sc. degree in Chemical Science in 2019 from Hyderabad University, India. She is currently pursuing her PhD. under the supervision of Prof. Madhab C. Das at the Indian Institute of Technology, Kharagpur, India. Her research interests are related to synthesis and characterization of robust metal–organic frameworks for suitable application in gas sorption, separation and proton conduction.
Debolina Mukherjee was born in West Bengal, India. She received her B.Sc. (Honours) degree in Chemistry from Lady Brabourne College, University of Calcutta, India in 2016. She received her M.Sc. (Chemistry) degree in June 2018 from Indian Institute of technology (ISM) Dhanbad. Debolina has joined Framework Lab in July, 2019 as a Junior Research fellow under the supervision of Prof. Madhab C. Das in the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Kharagpur for her PhD research work. Her thesis work focuses on the designs and synthesis of Metal–Organic Frameworks (MOFs) for their suitable potential application in ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ separation from gas mixtures, hydrocarbon separations and proton conduction.
Madhab C. Das was born in Midnapore, India. He received his B.S. (2002) from Midnapore College and M.S. (2004) in Chemistry from Vidyasagar University. He completed his Ph.D. in Supramolecular Chemistry at IIT Kanpur under the supervision of Professor P.K. Bharadwaj (2009). Then, he worked with Professors Banglin Chen at the University of Texas at San Antonio, George K.H. Shimizu at University of Calgary, and Hiroshi Kitagawa at Kyoto University as postdoctoral fellow (2009–2013) before joining IIT Kharagpur as Assistant Professor in 2013. Since 2019, he is an Associate Professor at IIT Kharagpur. His work is focused on functional MOFs.
